    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSituated in the vibrant rural community of Beaghmore this property offers much in terms of location and accommodation. First impressions are deceptive when it comes to this house as first impressions give no hint of the size and quality of the space inside.The bright front porch area leads into the spacious entrance hall. To the left of the hallway is a generous sitting room with carpet floors and dual aspect windows. To the right hand side of the house is a large bedroom with fitted wardrobes. Another door to the left opens into a fine sized living room with open fireplace and solid wooden floors. Further down the hallway you will find an open plan kitchen/dining room with vibrant kitchen units and a convenient island which comfortably seats three. This room which is south-west facing occupies the full width to the back of the house and has natural light from dual aspect. The utility is well fitted and provides rear access to the house. Just off the kitchen is a conservatory with glass windows where you can relax with a good book. Three more double bedrooms, an additional room currently in use as an office and a shower room completes the ground floor accommodation. A good sized bathroom with a separate bath with shower serves the bedrooms.The house is situated on a 0.48 acre site. It has mature trees and hedging surrounding the property provides privacy for the new owners. It has a wall to the front and blocked two-bay garage off the house to the rear with a spacious garden area to the rear and side of the property. Located close to the villages of Belclare & Caherlistrane. Tuam only 10 mins drive, Galway City only 25 mins drive. Viewing is highly recommended and by appointment only through Sherry FitzGerald Todd 09326622"
      },
